Description: safety layer for your terminal
 SafeShell rates every command you run by how reversible it is, tries it in
 a rootless sandbox first to show what it would really change, blocks the
 dangerous ones with a reason and a safer alternative, and keeps a snapshot
 so the last approved command can be undone and verified.
 .
 It hooks into bash and zsh. An optional assistant turns plain English into
 commands, using a local model that SafeShell downloads only when asked, or
 your own Claude, GPT or Gemini API key. The assistant can only make a
 command look riskier, never safer.
